#N canvas 20 20 2400 2150 12;
#X text 20 20 m_volca -- the Korg Volca FM \, and the only file allowed to talk to it. It is the FIRST OUTPUT-ONLY m_ layer in this project: the Volca transmits NOTHING AT ALL \, so unlike m_nano \, m_launchpad and m_organelle there are no device events to decode and nothing is ever published to param. The prefix still reads correctly -- m_ means the file that OWNS this device \, and m_launchpad already drives its own surface., f 84;
#X text 20 150 creation arg 1: the Pd channel that the Volca's OWN channel 1 lands on -- 49 on the Organelle \, which is input/output slot 4 per .pdsettings. REQUIRED. inlet 1: ONE inlet \, selector-prefixed -- notes <note> <vel> <dur> \, cc <controller> <value> \, program <n>. outlets: none \, this is a terminus., f 84;
#X text 20 250 WIRED \, NOT SENT \, AND ONE CORD RATHER THAN THREE. u_map reaches this file through a cord from u_root rather than a global bus: param is device-to-map and disp is display \, neither fits a sounding note \, and adding a name to the allowlist is a change to C-2 rather than a local call. The message is SELECTOR-PREFIXED for the same reason state carries three selectors on one name -- a device that learns a new capability costs ONE route argument here and nothing in u_map \, u_root or the conventions., f 84;
#X obj 20 460 inlet;
#X obj 20 540 route notes cc program;
#X obj 20 660 unpack f f f;
#X obj 20 800 makenote;
#X obj 20 1000 noteout;
#X obj 460 660 unpack f f;
#X obj 460 740 t b f;
#X obj 460 830 f;
#X obj 460 1000 ctlout;
#X obj 900 660 + 1;
#X obj 900 1000 pgmout;
#X obj 1300 660 t b;
#X msg 1300 730 fail m_volca bad-selector;
#X obj 1300 800 s err;
#X obj 1780 900 loadbang;
#X obj 1780 950 f \$1;
#X obj 1780 1000 t f f f;
#X text 1780 1060 THE CHANNEL GOES IN COLD \, off the RIGHTMOST outlets \, so all three destinations hold it before any value can arrive. Item 63 proved this pattern for midiout -- the port set into the cold inlet at load -- and it is used here for the same reason: Pd 0.49 does NOT warn about extra creation arguments \, so a clean load would prove nothing at all about a channel passed as an arg., f 60;
#X text 20 1080 unpack fires RIGHT TO LEFT \, so duration and velocity are stored in makenote before the note number triggers it. makenote owns the note-offs \, which is what stops a dropped cord or a reload leaving the Volca droning., f 60;
#X text 460 1100 ⚠️ THE t b f IS LOAD-BEARING AND THE OBVIOUS WIRING IS WRONG. ctlout takes value in the HOT inlet and controller in the cold one \, but unpack emits its RIGHTMOST outlet first -- so wiring value straight through would fire ctlout while it still held the PREVIOUS controller number \, sending every CC to the wrong destination. Silent \, plausible \, and wrong. The value is parked in the f \, the controller is set from t's right outlet \, and only then does the bang release it., f 56;
#X text 900 1080 ✅ MEASURED \, AND IT IS 1-BASED -- item 228. pgmout N puts wire value N-1 on the cable \, so the + 1 above is what makes this inlet mean the WIRE number that Korg \, Pajen and every prior test in this project use. Proved in BOTH directions on the hardware: pgmout 20 selected the patch raw 0xC0 19 selects \, and pgmout 21 selected the patch raw 0xC0 20 selects and STAYED on it through three raw interleaves. Without the + 1 every patch selected here would sit one BELOW the number asked for \, silently -- the 47+n shape exactly \, items 190 and 226., f 60;
#X text 1300 870 ⛔ THE REJECT IS A REAL ERROR \, WHICH IS THE OPPOSITE OF u_map's. An unrecognised selector means u_map and this file disagree about the interface \, and there is no other way to find out -- the Volca transmits nothing \, so a message that goes nowhere is indistinguishable from one that worked. The t b is the reject-outlet rule: a reject carries the DATA that failed to match \, never a bang., f 66;
#X text 20 1300 WHAT IS NOT HERE: aftertouch and pitch bend \, which the Volca ignores in any firmware \; and any notion of what a note MEANS -- this file is told what to play and plays it. ⛔ CLOCK AND TRANSPORT ARE NOT HERE EITHER \, AND THEY DO NOT REACH THIS DEVICE AT ALL. An earlier version of this comment said they were u_tempo's and "already reach every port". They reach TWO: u_tempo's realtime-out holds exactly two midiout objects \, set at loadbang to ports 1 and 3 -- the Launchpad and the SP-404. The Volca is port 4 and the nano is port 2 \, so neither has ever had a clock byte from this instrument. Measured with aseqdump on the hardware 2026-08-10 \, item 279: five seconds on Pd's Midi-Out 4 produced nothing at all. ⚠️ THAT MEANS THE VOLCA CANNOT SYNC \, which is a gap rather than a decision -- see plan-v04.md., f 84;
#X text 900 1300 ⚠️ REQUIRES PAJEN 1.09 FIRMWARE for velocity and program change -- and BOTH are gated behind global settings that no secondary source documents. Md UEL On \, PCMId On \, PCnot OFF. See ref/device/volca.md., f 60;
#X text 1300 380 ONE INLET \, THREE SELECTORS. route matches a SELECTOR \, so notes 48 100 200 arrives with notes as the selector and 48 100 200 as the remainder -- and a remainder starting with a float really is a list \, which is why unpack takes it with no list append in front. program <n> leaves a lone float \, which is what + 1 wants., f 76;
#X obj 20 1700 loadbang;
#X obj 20 1750 del 2000;
#X obj 20 1800 f \$1;
#X obj 20 1850 print m_volca-channel;
#X text 300 1750 SELF-IDENTIFYING \, the same way m_nano is. The Volca transmits NOTHING \, so a wrong channel here is invisible from every direction: no readback \, no error \, and Pd 0.49 does not warn about a missing creation argument. This print is the only thing that says out loud which channel this instance actually got. ⚠️ THE 2000 ms IS NOT COSMETIC -- tools/deploy.sh gates on OUTPUT rather than exit status \, and its check quits at about 735 ms \, so a print at loadbang would fail every deploy., f 66;
#X obj 1400 1440 loadbang;
#X msg 1400 1500 expect m_volca none;
#X obj 1400 1560 s presence;
#X text 1750 1440 ⛔ none IS A KIND \, AND SAYING IT OUT LOUD IS THE WHOLE POINT. This file's own header already says the Volca transmits NOTHING AT ALL -- that is what makes it the one output-only m_ layer -- so there is no evidence of its presence for any amount of code to find. It registers and stops there: no c_presence \, no poll \, no ageing \, and it can never be declared lost or back. ⚠️ UNDETECTABLE IS A FACT AND NOT A GAP \, and the difference is worth three boxes because the alternative is a silence that reads as an oversight -- somebody forgot m_volca \, rather than somebody established that m_volca cannot be watched. RECOVERY IS STILL REAL HERE: u_present re-runs wire.sh for the WHOLE rig whenever any source is lost \, so a replugged Volca does come back with everything else. Nothing in the patch can confirm that it did \, which is why its bench step is judged by ear. See ref/module/presence.md., f 44;
